# Code owners. The last matching line wins, so every line below repeats @mikker.
#
# The maintainer owns everything: shared tooling, docs, CI, the workspace, the Makefile, the README
# and every first-party extension. First-party extensions have no line of their own.
* @mikker

# Contributed extensions: the folder and the extension's own store media are co-owned by the
# original author, so updates confined to them can be approved by either owner.
# When admitting a new extension, add its three lines here, in alphabetical order:
#
#   /<Name>Extension/              @mikker @<author>
#   /media/screenshots/<slug>/     @mikker @<author>
#   /media/icons/<slug>.*          @mikker @<author>
#
# The author must have write access to the repository, or GitHub ignores their entry.

# Strongbox — Denis Maier (#8)
/StrongboxExtension/ @mikker @denMaier
/media/screenshots/strongbox/ @mikker @denMaier
/media/icons/strongbox.* @mikker @denMaier
